section.body date.updated="0"><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0">The climate &ldquo;pillar&rdquo; policy initiatives and priority actions along with support for aspects of the other pillars in the <ital>Made-in-Manitoba Plan</ital> were put into action with the enactment of <ital>The Climate and Green Plan Act</ital><footnote date.updated="0"><footnote.reference date.updated="0">1</footnote.reference><footnote.body date.updated="0"><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0"><ital>The Climate and Green Plan Act</ital>, C.C.S.M., c. C134.</para.text></para></footnote.body></footnote> on November 8, 2018 (&ldquo;<ital>The 2018 Climate and Green Plan Act</ital>&rdquo;).</para.text></para><head align="l" toc.include="y" date.updated="0"><name.block toc.include="y" date.updated="0"><name date.updated="0"><bold>Purpose of <ital>The 2018 Climate and Green Plan Act</ital></bold></name></name.block></head><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0">The preamble to the Act first recognizes that &ldquo;climate change is the result of greenhouse gas emissions&rdquo; primarily caused by &ldquo;the use of carbon-based fuels and processes that release carbon&rdquo; creating a wide range of risks and challenges locally and globally.<footnote date.updated="0"><footnote.reference date.updated="0">2</footnote.reference><footnote.body date.updated="0"><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0"><ital>The Climate and Green Plan Act</ital>, C.C.S.M., c. C134, Preamble.</para.text></para></footnote.body></footnote> On that underpinning, the preamble goes on to state that a &ldquo;move to a low carbon economy is critical to slowing climate change and minimizing its effects&rdquo;, emphasizing that economic development must balance human and environmental interests. In so doing, and consistent with the envisioned <ital>Made-in-Manitoba</ital> pillars, the preamble describes the government&apos;s commitment to &ldquo;address climate change, promote sustainable development, and protect and enhance water resources, natural habitat and biodiversity&rdquo;.<footnote date.updated="0"><footnote.reference date.updated="0">3</footnote.reference><footnote.body date.updated="0"><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0"><ital>The Climate and Green Plan Act</ital>, C.C.S.M., c. C134, Preamble.</para.text></para></footnote.body></footnote></para.text></para><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0">The Act defines &ldquo;sustainable development&rdquo; as: &ldquo;development that meets the needs of the present generation without compromising the ability of future generations to meet their needs&rdquo;.<footnote date.updated="0"><footnote.reference date.updated="0">4</footnote.reference><footnote.body date.updated="0"><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0"><ital>The Climate and Green Plan Act</ital>, C.C.S.M., c. C134, s. 1.</para.text></para></footnote.body></footnote></para.text></para><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0">Along with the imposition of specific requirements and consequential amendments as discussed in this chapter, the Act creates a framework for regulations by which additional or more specific actions may be developed. For example, the Act permits the Lieutenant Governor in Council to establish regulations to prescribe a gas or substance to be a &ldquo;greenhouse gas&rdquo; for the purposes of the Act.<footnote date.updated="0"><footnote.reference date.updated="0">5</footnote.reference><footnote.body date.updated="0"><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0"><ital>The Climate and Green Plan Act</ital>, C.C.S.M., c. C134, s. 12(a). &ldquo;Greenhouse gas&rdquo; is currently defined in the act as: &ldquo;carbon dioxide, methane, nitrous oxide, sulphur hexafluoride and the prescribed categories of hydrofluorocarbons and perfluorocarbons, and includes any other gas or substance or category of gas or substance prescribed by regulation to be a greenhouse gas. <ital>The Climate and Green Plan Act</ital>, C.C.S.M., c. C134, s. 1.</para.text></para></footnote.body></footnote> The Lieutenant Governor may also prescribe the government &ldquo;agencies&rdquo; or &ldquo;entities&rdquo; tasked with reducing GHG emissions and improving sustainable operations within government activities<footnote date.updated="0"><footnote.reference date.updated="0">6</footnote.reference><footnote.body date.updated="0"><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0"><ital>The Climate and Green Plan Act</ital>, C.C.S.M., c. C134, ss. 12(b) and 10(1)-(2).</para.text></para></footnote.body></footnote> and may define <?WGXPPrightHandPageStart sp=";;47" nep=";;49" hyphenated="y" folio="8-47" backFolio="8-48" backBlank="n" releaseNumber="4" releaseDate="2022;12;30" ?>any word or expression used but not defined in the Act.<footnote date.updated="0"><footnote.reference date.updated="0">7</footnote.reference><footnote.body date.updated="0"><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0"><ital>The Climate and Green Plan Act</ital>, C.C.S.M., c. C134, s. 12(c).</para.text></para></footnote.body></footnote> The Act also gives the Lieutenant Governor in Council broad, general powers to make regulations respecting any matter considered necessary or advisable for carrying out the purpose of the Act. At the time of writing there were no regulations pursuant to the Act.</para.text></para><head align="l" toc.include="y" date.updated="0"><name.block toc.include="y" date.updated="0"><name date.updated="0"><bold>Provisions Related to the Climate and Green Plan</bold></name></name.block></head><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0">Section 2 of the Act empowers the Minister tasked with the administration of the Act to develop a &ldquo;Climate and Green Plan&rdquo;. The plan must be a &ldquo;comprehensive framework of programs, policies and measures&rdquo; to reduce GHG emissions and address the effects of climate change and promote sustainable development.<footnote date.updated="0"><footnote.reference date.updated="0">8</footnote.reference><footnote.body date.updated="0"><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0"><ital>The Climate and Green Plan Act</ital>, C.C.S.M., c. C134, ss. 2(1)(a) and (b).</para.text></para></footnote.body></footnote></para.text></para><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0">Consistent with the preamble of the Act, as well as the four &ldquo;pillars&rdquo; and vision of a comprehensive, integrated framework under the <ital>Made-in-Manitoba Plan</ital>, the plan under s. 2 of the Act must also improve the management and protection of Manitoba&apos;s water resources and preserve and protect Manitoba&apos;s natural habitat and biodiversity.<footnote date.updated="0"><footnote.reference date.updated="0">9</footnote.reference><footnote.body date.updated="0"><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0"><ital>The Climate and Green Plan Act</ital>, C.C.S.M., c. C134, s. 2(1)(c) and (d).</para.text></para></footnote.body></footnote></para.text></para><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0">When developing and implementing the plan, the Minister must take into account the advice and recommendations of the &ldquo;Expert Advisory Council&rdquo; established under the Act (discussed further below) and must conduct an annual review of the &ldquo;programs, policies and measures&rdquo; to determine if they are achieving their intended goals.<footnote date.updated="0"><footnote.reference date.updated="0">10</footnote.reference><footnote.body date.updated="0"><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0"><ital>The Climate and Green Plan Act</ital>, C.C.S.M., c. C134, s. 2(2) and (3).</para.text></para></footnote.body></footnote></para.text></para><head align="l" toc.include="y" date.updated="0"><name.block toc.include="y" date.updated="0"><name date.updated="0"><bold>Provisions Related to GHG Emissions Reduction Goals and the Carbon Savings Account</bold></name></name.block></head><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0">Pursuant to s. 3, the Minister, on the advice and recommendation of the Expert Advisory Council, must establish GHG emissions reductions goals in five-year periods, with the first five-year period running from 2018-2022.<footnote date.updated="0"><footnote.reference date.updated="0">11</footnote.reference><footnote.body date.updated="0"><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0"><ital>The Climate and Green Plan Act</ital>, C.C.S.M., c. C134, s. 3(1) and (2).</para.text></para></footnote.body></footnote> Following the 2018-2022 goal (established within the first year of the coming into force of the Act), the goal for each subsequent five-year period is to be established by the Minister before the start of each period.<footnote date.updated="0"><footnote.reference date.updated="0">12</footnote.reference><footnote.body date.updated="0"><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0"><ital>The Climate and Green Plan Act</ital>, C.C.S.M., c. C134, s. 3(3). Note that in October 2021, the Minister tasked the Expert Advisory Council to provide advice and recommendations on emission reduction targets for the next carbon savings account 2023-2027. See letter from the Minister of Conservation and Climate to the Expert Advisory Council (October 5, 2021).</para.text></para></footnote.body></footnote></para.text></para><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0">GHG emission reduction goals are subject to &ldquo;adjustment&rdquo; in the event the reduction goal from a previous five-year period has not been met.<footnote date.updated="0"><footnote.reference date.updated="0">13</footnote.reference><footnote.body date.updated="0"><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0"><ital>The Climate and Green Plan Act</ital>, C.C.S.M., c. C134, s. 4(2).</para.text></para></footnote.body></footnote> Whether an adjustment is required is dependent on the &ldquo;carbon savings account&rdquo; balance.</para.text></para><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0">The &ldquo;carbon savings account&rdquo; established under s. 4 of the Act keeps a running balance of the GHG emissions reductions achieved in a five-year period in comparison to the emissions reduction goals set for those periods.<footnote date.updated="0"><footnote.reference date.updated="0">14</footnote.reference><footnote.body date.updated="0"><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0"><ital>The Climate and Green Plan Act</ital>, C.C.S.M., c. C134, s. 4(1).</para.text></para></footnote.body></footnote> When GHG emissions reduction goals have not been met in a preceding five-year period, the shortfall from that five-year period is to be &ldquo;added&rdquo; to the emissions reduction goal in the subsequent five-year period.<footnote date.updated="0"><footnote.reference date.updated="0">15</footnote.reference><footnote.body date.updated="0"><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0"><ital>The Climate and Green Plan Act</ital>, C.C.S.M., c. C134, s. 4(2).</para.text></para></footnote.body></footnote></para.text></para><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0">Pursuant to s. 8 of the Act, when providing advice and recommendations to the Minister respecting GHG emissions reductions goals, the Expert Advisory Council must have regard to:<footnote date.updated="0"><footnote.reference date.updated="0">16</footnote.reference><footnote.body date.updated="0"><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0"><ital>The Climate and Green Plan Act</ital>, C.C.S.M., c. C134, s. 8(2).</para.text></para></footnote.body></footnote></para.text><list list.style="block" date.updated="0"><list.item date.updated="0"><name.block toc.include="y" date.updated="0"><designator date.updated="0">(a)</designator></name.block><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0">the total projected GHG emissions for that five-year period, if no new GHG emissions reductions measures are implemented in that period;</para.text></para></list.item><list.item date.updated="0"><name.block toc.include="y" date.updated="0"><designator date.updated="0">(b)</designator></name.block><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0">economic, industrial and demographic projections;</para.text></para></list.item><list.item date.updated="0"><name.block toc.include="y" date.updated="0"><designator date.updated="0">(c)</designator></name.block><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0">the implementation of GHG emissions reduction measures;</para.text></para></list.item><list.item date.updated="0"><name.block toc.include="y" date.updated="0"><designator date.updated="0">(d)</designator></name.block><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0">the availability and use of new and emerging technologies; and</para.text></para></list.item><list.item date.updated="0"><name.block toc.include="y" date.updated="0"><designator date.updated="0">(e)</designator></name.block><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0">any other considerations the council considers relevant.</para.text></para></list.item></list></para><head align="l" toc.include="y" date.updated="0"><name.block toc.include="y" date.updated="0"><name date.updated="0"><bold>Provisions Related to the Expert Advisory Council</bold></name></name.block></head><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0">Section 7 of the Act establishes the Expert Advisory Council and its mandate. In addition to providing advice and recommendations to the Minister respecting GHG emissions reduction goals,<footnote date.updated="0"><footnote.reference date.updated="0">17</footnote.reference><footnote.body date.updated="0"><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0"><ital>The Climate and Green Plan Act</ital>, C.C.S.M., c. C134, s. 8(1)(c). See previous heading in this chapter for list of &ldquo;Section 8&rdquo; factors that the Expert Advisory Council must take into account when advising or recommending GHG emissions reductions goals.</para.text></para></footnote.body></footnote> the Expert Advisory Council is to provide the Minister with advice and recommendations on &ldquo;programs, poli<?WGXPPrightHandPageStart sp=";;49" nep=";;51" hyphenated="n" folio="8-49" backFolio="8-50" backBlank="n" releaseNumber="4" releaseDate="2022;12;30" ?>cies and measures&rdquo; to be included in the plan, review progress on the plan&apos;s implementation, and provide advice on any required changes.<footnote date.updated="0"><footnote.reference date.updated="0">18</footnote.reference><footnote.body date.updated="0"><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0"><ital>The Climate and Green Plan Act</ital>, C.C.S.M., c. C134, ss. 8(1)(a) and (b).</para.text></para></footnote.body></footnote></para.text></para><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0">The Expert Advisory Council is permitted to establish subcommittees to perform specific duties and functions as well as the council&apos;s procedural rules and those of the subcommittees.<footnote date.updated="0"><footnote.reference date.updated="0">19</footnote.reference><footnote.body date.updated="0"><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0"><ital>The Climate and Green Plan Act</ital>, C.C.S.M., c. C134, ss. 7(2) and (3).</para.text></para></footnote.body></footnote></para.text></para><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0">The Act empowers the Minister to appoint to the Expert Advisory Council, persons the Minister &ldquo;considers appropriate to an independent expert advisory council&rdquo;.<footnote date.updated="0"><footnote.reference date.updated="0">20</footnote.reference><footnote.body date.updated="0"><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0"><ital>The Climate and Green Plan Act</ital>, C.C.S.M., c. C134, s. 7(1).</para.text></para></footnote.body></footnote></para.text></para><head align="l" toc.include="y" date.updated="0"><name.block toc.include="y" date.updated="0"><name date.updated="0"><bold>Provisions Related to the Low Carbon Government Office</bold></name></name.block></head><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0">Section 9 of the Act establishes the Low Carbon Government Office (the &ldquo;LCGO&rdquo;), whose mandate is to develop and implement &ldquo;policies, strategies and initiatives&rdquo; to reduce GHG emissions and promote sustainable operations by government departments (or other government agencies or entities established pursuant to regulations under the Act).<footnote date.updated="0"><footnote.reference date.updated="0">21</footnote.reference><footnote.body date.updated="0"><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0"><ital>The Climate and Green Plan Act</ital>, C.C.S.M., c. C134, s. 10(1).</para.text></para></footnote.body></footnote></para.text></para><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0">The Act requires the LCGO to focus on the following areas of activity:<footnote date.updated="0"><footnote.reference date.updated="0">22</footnote.reference><footnote.body date.updated="0"><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0"><ital>The Climate and Green Plan Act</ital>, C.C.S.M., c. C134, s. 10(2).</para.text></para></footnote.body></footnote></para.text><list list.style="block" date.updated="0"><list.item date.updated="0"><name.block toc.include="y" date.updated="0"><designator date.updated="0">(a)</designator></name.block><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0">sustainable procurement of goods and services;</para.text></para></list.item><list.item date.updated="0"><name.block toc.include="y" date.updated="0"><designator date.updated="0">(b)</designator></name.block><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0">improved building design, construction and management;</para.text></para></list.item><list.item date.updated="0"><name.block toc.include="y" date.updated="0"><designator date.updated="0">(c)</designator></name.block><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0">increased use of zero emission vehicles and reduced fuel consumption in government vehicle and equipment fleets;</para.text></para></list.item><list.item date.updated="0"><name.block toc.include="y" date.updated="0"><designator date.updated="0">(d)</designator></name.block><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0">innovative use and management of information and communication technologies; and</para.text></para></list.item><list.item date.updated="0"><name.block toc.include="y" date.updated="0"><designator date.updated="0">(e)</designator></name.block><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0">improved waste reduction and management operations.</para.text></para></list.item></list></para><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0">The LCGO must also track and record the GHG emissions of all government departments (or other government agencies or entities established pursuant to regulations under the Act) on an annual basis.<footnote date.updated="0"><footnote.reference date.updated="0">23</footnote.reference><footnote.body date.updated="0"><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0"><ital>The Climate and Green Plan Act</ital>, C.C.S.M., c. C134, s. 10(3).</para.text></para></footnote.body></footnote></para.text></para><head align="l" toc.include="y" date.updated="0"><name.block toc.include="y" date.updated="0"><name date.updated="0"><bold>Provisions related to the Made-in-Manitoba Climate and Green Fund</bold></name></name.block></head><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0">Section 11 of the Act establishes the <ital>Made-in-Manitoba Climate and Green Fund</ital> (the &ldquo;Fund&rdquo;). The Fund is a continuation of the Sustainable Development Innovations Fund that was established under <ital>The Sustainable Development Act</ital> (which was repealed by the Act).</para.text></para><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0">The purpose of the Fund is to provide financial support for &ldquo;projects, studies and activities&rdquo; that &ldquo;will do one or more of the following&rdquo;:<footnote date.updated="0"><footnote.reference date.updated="0">24</footnote.reference><footnote.body date.updated="0"><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0"><ital>The Climate and Green Plan Act</ital>, C.C.S.M., c. C134, s. 11(2).</para.text></para></footnote.body></footnote></para.text><list list.style="block" date.updated="0"><list.item date.updated="0"><name.block toc.include="y" date.updated="0"><designator date.updated="0">(a)</designator></name.block><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0">reduce greenhouse gas emissions;</para.text></para></list.item><list.item date.updated="0"><name.block toc.include="y" date.updated="0"><designator date.updated="0">(b)</designator></name.block><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0">address the effects of climate change, including measures to adapt to climate change;</para.text></para></list.item><list.item date.updated="0"><name.block toc.include="y" date.updated="0"><designator date.updated="0">(c)</designator></name.block><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0">promote sustainable development;</para.text></para></list.item><list.item date.updated="0"><name.block toc.include="y" date.updated="0"><designator date.updated="0">(d)</designator></name.block><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0">improve the management and protection of water resources;</para.text></para></list.item><list.item date.updated="0"><name.block toc.include="y" date.updated="0"><designator date.updated="0">(e)</designator></name.block><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0">preserve and protect Manitoba&apos;s water resources, natural habitat and biodiversity.</para.text></para></list.item></list></para><head align="l" toc.include="y" date.updated="0"><name.block toc.include="y" date.updated="0"><name date.updated="0"><bold>Provisions Related to Reporting</bold></name></name.block></head><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0">Pursuant to sections 5 and 6 of the Act respectively, the Minister must prepare an &ldquo;Annual report&rdquo; and a &ldquo;Five-year report&rdquo;.</para.text></para><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0">The Annual report must report on programs, policies and measures employed in that year and include the following information: GHG emissions reductions achieved, if any; applicable emissions reduction goals and status of the carbon savings account; Expert Advisory Council activity summary; Low Carbon Government Office activity summary including GHG emissions report of all applicable government entities for that year; a &ldquo;Made-in-Manitoba Climate and Green Fund&rdquo; activities report, including a list of those receiving money and projects, studies or activities supported by the fund.<footnote date.updated="0"><footnote.reference date.updated="0">25</footnote.reference><footnote.body date.updated="0"><para date.updated="0"><para.text date.updated="0"><ital>The Climate and Green Plan Act</ital>, C.C.S.M., c. C134, s. 5(1)-(6).</para.text></para></footnote.body></footnote></para.text></para><